    {
      "name": "words",
      "displayName": "What these words mean",
      "pageType": "PAGE_TYPE_CANVAS",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "word_list",
            "textbox_spec": "# What these words mean\n\n- **Flagged payment**: A payment the model ranked among the 50 most suspicious of its hour, so a person should look at it.\n- **Case**: The review of one flagged payment. It stays open until its verdict is recorded.\n- **Verdict**: The answer to a case: confirmed fraud or false alarm. It arrives 3 simulated days after the payment.\n- **Confirmed fraud**: A flagged payment that really was fraud.\n- **False alarm**: A flagged payment that turned out to be honest.\n- **Simulated hour**: One hour of the replayed month of payments, numbered from 1 to 743.\n- **Model version**: Which saved copy of the fraud model made the decision. Each new copy gets the next number.\n- **Champion model**: The model version currently trusted to score new payments.\n- **Risk score**: How suspicious the model found a payment. Higher is more suspicious. It ranks payments, it is not a chance.\n- **Rejected row**: A payment record that failed a basic check, such as an amount below zero, and was set aside.\n- **Job run**: One run of the scheduled work that releases, loads, cleans, scores and flags payments.\n- **Task**: One step inside a job run, such as loading or scoring.\n- **REDACTED**: Shown instead of an account name to people who may not see who paid whom."
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 6,
            "height": 10
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
